<section class="how">
    <h2>How to Calculate Business Days</h2>
    <p>Calculating the exact number of working days between two dates is highly critical for legal contract deadlines, employee timesheets, shipping calculations, and invoice payment terms. Standard business days count Monday through Friday, skipping Saturday and Sunday.</p>
    
    <h3>Steps to Count Working Days</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Identify your starting date and ending date. Deciding whether you should include the start date in the final tally depends on your contract phrasing (e.g. "commencing on" includes the day itself).</li>
        <li>Count the total number of calendar days in the period.</li>
        <li>Subtract all weekends (Saturday and Sunday). For every complete week, subtract exactly two days.</li>
        <li>Check for any recognized public or bank holidays that fall on a weekday within that range and subtract them. If a holiday falls on a Saturday or Sunday, check whether it is officially observed on the neighboring Monday or Friday.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>Using our interactive tool speeds up this process and prevents calculation errors. You can toggle between United States federal holidays or United Kingdom bank holidays to automatically screen out days when financial institutions and courts are closed.</p>
</section>

<section class="formula">
    <h2>Working Day Equations and Calendar Logic</h2>
    <p>To calculate calendar days to business days manually, you can use the following mathematical approximation before subtracting specific public holidays:</p>
    <p><strong>Business Days &approx; (Calendar Days &times; 5) / 7</strong></p>
    <p>For high-precision operations, developers and financial operations use calendar-matching algorithms. For example, to add business days programmatically:</p>
    <pre style="background:var(--input-bg); padding:1rem; border-radius:6px; overflow-x:auto; font-size:0.9rem; border:1px solid var(--border);">
let date = new Date(startDate);
while (daysToAdd > 0) {
    date.setDate(date.getDate() + 1);
    if (isBusinessDay(date)) {
        daysToAdd--;
    }
}
return date;</pre>
    <p>Our tool runs this exact loop on every recalculation, ensuring that leap years, varying month lengths, and multi-year ranges are completely accounted for without rounding issues.</p>
</section>

