<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    
    <h3>What is the difference between working days and business days?</h3>
    <p>In most commercial contexts, the terms are interchangeable. Both define days of the week on which normal business operations are conducted (usually Monday through Friday) excluding Saturdays, Sundays, and public bank holidays. In some specific industries (like retail, shipping, or healthcare), working days may include Saturdays or Sundays if staff is actively scheduled.</p>

    <h3>How many business days are in a typical year?</h3>
    <p>A standard calendar year of 365 days has either 261 or 262 weekdays. After subtracting 10 to 11 standard national public holidays, there are typically between 250 and 252 business days in a year depending on weekends and leap years.</p>

    <h3>Does a bank holiday count as a business day?</h3>
    <p>No. Standard financial transactions, bank clearances (such as ACH transfers), and court deadlines do not count bank holidays. If your contract payment deadline lands on an official bank holiday, the transaction is processed on the next available business day.</p>

    <h3>How do I calculate 10 business days from today?</h3>
    <p>Set the start date to today's date in our "Add/Subtract Days" mode, select "Add (+)", and input 10. The calculator will automatically jump past the next two weekends and any intermediate public holidays, showing the exact calendar date of your deadline.</p>
